course: dictionary
lesson: 15489
title: Strumming along
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: To strum is to play a guitar or ukulele by brushing your fingers or a pick across the strings. You can find the meaning by reading the words around it. «Maya strummed her ukulele while the class sang.» The ukulele and the singing are the clues, so strum must be a way of playing music.
explain: Strum can also be a noun. «Ben played one strum, and the whole room went quiet.» Here a strum is one brush across the strings, and the sound it makes. Always check your meaning by putting it into the sentence and seeing if it still makes sense.
explain: Strumming often sets a mood. «The guitarist strummed a dreamy tune as the sun went down.» The slow, gentle strumming makes the scene feel calm. Words like this help you picture what is happening, even if you have never held a guitar.
fact: Strum means to brush your fingers or a pick across the strings of an instrument like a guitar or ukulele.
fact: As a noun, a strum is one brush across the strings, or the sound it makes.
fact: Strum a chord means to play several strings together to make one chord.
fact: A strumming pattern is a set order of strums, such as down, down, up.
fact: Strum along means to play your instrument with other people who are already playing.
exercise: «Maya strummed her ukulele while the class sang.» What does strummed mean? | Tuned the strings very slowly | *Brushed her fingers across the strings | Put the ukulele away in its case | Hit the ukulele with a hammer
exercise: «Ben played one strum, and the whole room went quiet.» What is a strum here? | A loud shout | A kind of guitar case | A long song with many verses | *One brush across the strings
exercise: Which of these is a strumming pattern? | *Down, down, up | Hop, skip, jump | Red, blue, green | Loud, soft, loud
test: «The guitarist strummed a dreamy tune as the sun went down.» What mood does the strumming create? | Scared and tense | Busy and rushed | Angry and loud | *Relaxed and dreamy
test: In class, the teacher says, «Everyone, strum along!» What does she want you to do? | Sing a song without any music | Hide your instrument under your chair | Stop playing and leave the room | *Play your ukulele with the others
exam: Which sentence uses strum correctly? | Sam strummed a sandwich for his lunch | Sam strummed the bus to school | Sam strummed the door shut loudly | *Sam strummed three chords on his ukulele
